ure" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=2x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-6,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4db46a9d62f9a21d8f80a9f94b90e4fb4fe87c5b80b813f4fc9c8610a9418521" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}x"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/