is" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-4,-1)$ and passes through the point $(5,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (2+1)^{2} & =4p(5+4) \\\\ 9 & =36p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{4})(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4db46a9d62f9a21d8f80a9f94b90e4fb4fe87c5b80b813f4fc9c8610a9418521" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y+1)^{2}=-(x+4)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/state.json" "file_sha256" "cbb323e2e80fffcb5b3d5b27ed767c90db63e4d5a7e12621e7c9826cf4a83901" "basis" 619 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y+1)^{2}=-2(x+4)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/C