Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-4,-1)$ and passes through the point $(5,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (2+1)^{2} & =4p(5+4) \\\\ 9 & =36p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{4})(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc3f79a138a915cb92881b754592e6e64a4322a67c0cfce12b9664e757072c25"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(y+1)^{2}=-(x+4)"] ["math" "(y+1)^{2}=-2(x+4)"] ["math" "(y+1)^{2}=2(x+4)"] ["math" "(y+1)^{2}=x+4"] ["math" "(y+4)^{2}=x+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-11800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y+1)^{2}=x+4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,-4),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 16 & =32p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc3f79a138a915cb92881b754592e6e64a4322a67c0cfce12b9664e757072c25"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{x}^{2}=2y"] ["math" "{x}^{2}=4y"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=-16x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=2x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115631" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{2}=2x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/assets/1f6330a6e9bc0e48326982c7b7509f3e2257de994c5736c813ede93a07491e70.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,-3),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 9 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cc3f79a138a915cb92881b754592e6e64a4322a67c0cfce12b9664e757072c25"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}y"] ["math" "(x-3)^{2}=3y"] ["math" "(y+3)^{2}=3x"] ["math" "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x"] ["math" "{y}^{2}=3(x+3)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115643" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(y+3)^{2}=3x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-3),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3-1) \\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{8})(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/state.json" "file_sha256" "c38cfcd1755319ab8b18641f82d0e03e40c90774c89fe44e7aaa5bd724e5324c"} {"question" "q-115646" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340